# Test Assertions and Test Data

Project-owned rule. It **overrides** the "Use xUnit's built-in assertions" and
"Avoid third-party assertion libraries" sections of `vendor/aaron-csharp-testing.md`,
which is kept verbatim for upstream re-sync. Authoritative source: constitution
Principle IX (`.specify/memory/constitution.md`).

## Libraries

| Concern | Use | Do not use |
|---|---|---|
| Assertions | **Shouldly** | FluentAssertions (paid commercial licence from v8); raw xUnit `Assert` except `Assert.Collection` |
| Mocking | **NSubstitute** | Moq |
| Anonymous test data | **AutoFixture** (`Fixture`, `[AutoData]`) | hand-rolled random values |
| Realistic fake values | **Faker.Net** | Bogus |

Adding a second assertion or mocking library is a defect.

## Assertions

Read as *actual should be expected*; Shouldly prints both values and the expression on failure.

```csharp
// arrange
var order = new Order(OrderId.New(), [new OrderLine("SKU1", 2, 10.0m)]);

// act
var total = order.CalculateTotal();

// assert
total.ShouldBe(20.0m);
order.Lines.ShouldHaveSingleItem().Sku.ShouldBe("SKU1");
Should.Throw<ArgumentException>(() => new Order(OrderId.New(), []))
    .Message.ShouldBe("Order must have at least one line");
```

Group related checks with `ShouldSatisfyAllConditions` so one run reports every failure:

```csharp
result.ShouldSatisfyAllConditions(
    r => r.IsSuccess.ShouldBeTrue(),
    r => r.OrderId.ShouldBe(order.Id),
    r => r.Errors.ShouldBeEmpty());
```

Common equivalents for the vendored xUnit examples:

| xUnit `Assert` | Shouldly |
|---|---|
| `Assert.Equal(e, a)` | `a.ShouldBe(e)` |
| `Assert.True(x)` / `Assert.False(x)` | `x.ShouldBeTrue()` / `x.ShouldBeFalse()` |
| `Assert.Null(x)` / `Assert.NotNull(x)` | `x.ShouldBeNull()` / `x.ShouldNotBeNull()` |
| `Assert.Contains(i, c)` / `Assert.DoesNotContain(i, c)` | `c.ShouldContain(i)` / `c.ShouldNotContain(i)` |
| `Assert.Empty(c)` / `Assert.NotEmpty(c)` | `c.ShouldBeEmpty()` / `c.ShouldNotBeEmpty()` |
| `Assert.Single(c)` | `c.ShouldHaveSingleItem()` |
| `Assert.All(c, x => …)` | `c.ShouldAllBe(x => …)` |
| `Assert.IsType<T>(x)` | `x.ShouldBeOfType<T>()` |
| `Assert.IsAssignableFrom<T>(x)` | `x.ShouldBeAssignableTo<T>()` |
| `Assert.Throws<T>(() => …)` | `Should.Throw<T>(() => …)` |
| `await Assert.ThrowsAsync<T>(…)` | `await Should.ThrowAsync<T>(…)` |
| `Assert.InRange(x, lo, hi)` | `x.ShouldBeInRange(lo, hi)` |
| `Assert.StartsWith` / `Assert.Matches` | `ShouldStartWith` / `ShouldMatch` |
| `Assert.Same` / `Assert.NotSame` | `ShouldBeSameAs` / `ShouldNotBeSameAs` |

`Assert.Collection` has no Shouldly equivalent for ordered, per-element lambdas and remains
the one permitted xUnit assertion; use Shouldly inside each element lambda.

## Mocking

```csharp
var repository = Substitute.For<IOrderRepository>();
repository.FindAsync(id, Arg.Any<CancellationToken>()).Returns(order);

await sut.ProcessAsync(id, TestContext.Current.CancellationToken);

await repository.Received(1).SaveAsync(order, Arg.Any<CancellationToken>());
```

Never mock infrastructure (database, broker, file system): use Testcontainers, WireMock.Net,
or `MockFileSystem` as the vendored rule already requires.

## Test data

- `AutoFixture` for values whose content does not matter to the test; `[Theory, AutoData]`
  when every parameter is anonymous.
- `Faker.Net` when a human-plausible value matters (titles, names, years, paths).
- Hand-written builders only for domain invariants AutoFixture cannot satisfy, such as a
  `Movie` that must already be in a specific `EnrichmentStatus`.
